    "blocks": [
      {
        "id": "summary",
        "type": "markdown",
        "body": "## Executive Summary\n\n- **The best model is an editorial one-property site, not a miniature OTA.** Indo House St. John, Leaping Lamb Farm, Independence River Lodge, Chalets Hygge, and Kinross House are the strongest overall references.\n- **Design should create desire first and remove doubt immediately after.** A cinematic or exceptional still hero, one visible “Book your stay” action, a compact facts panel, trusted reviews, and a short location story are the most reusable patterns.\n- **Guesty should remain the transaction layer.** The branded site should own discovery and persuasion, then hand dates, availability, price, terms, payment, and reservation completion to Guesty.\n- **The ranking is an editorial fit assessment, not conversion benchmarking.** Public sites do not expose comparable conversion data; scores emphasize transferability to one property."
      },
      {
        "id": "method",
        "type": "markdown",
        "body": "## How the shortlist was judged\n\nEach candidate was assessed on six weighted dimensions: visual identity (25%), booking-path clarity (20%), mobile and navigation simplicity (15%), trust and reassurance (15%), property storytelling (15%), and transferability to a one-property Guesty build (10%). The source pool combines vacation-rental roundups, boutique-hotel design roundups, direct-booking portfolios, and live property sites. Large brands were retained as pattern references but generally ranked below focused single-property examples."
      },
      {
        "id": "top_intro",
        "type": "markdown",
        "body": "## The top 30 favor focused, emotionally clear sites\n\nThe highest-ranked examples establish a distinct feeling in the first screen, keep choices limited, and make practical information easy to scan. For Central Island Home, the useful lesson is not to imitate a hotel’s feature count; it is to borrow its visual discipline and connect one decisive CTA to Guesty."
      },
      {
        "id": "top_chart",
        "type": "chart",
        "chartId": "top10chart"
      },
      {
        "id": "top_table",
        "type": "table",
        "tableId": "top30"
      },
      {
        "id": "blueprint",
        "type": "markdown",
        "body": "## Recommended blueprint for Central Island Home\n\n1. **Hero:** one exceptional property image or short optimized film, a specific one-line promise, and one primary booking CTA.\n2. **Quick-fit strip:** only facts already approved in `src/content.mjs`; do not invent amenities, beds, occupancy, ratings, distances, policies, or an exact address.\n3. **Stay story:** a short editorial sequence covering the home, the setting, and who the stay is for.\n4. **Photo narrative:** curated groups rather than an undifferentiated gallery.\n5. **Trust layer:** approved reviews or platform proof, host identity, secure-booking language, and transparent handoff to Guesty.\n6. **Local guide:** a small number of genuinely useful recommendations, written in the same voice as the property.\n7. **Guesty handoff:** availability, live pricing, terms, payment, and reservation completion stay in Guesty."
      },
      {
        "id": "next",
        "type": "markdown",
        "body": "## Recommended next steps\n\n- Choose one visual direction from the top five rather than blending all 30.\n- Build the homepage around one primary conversion path and one secondary “Explore the stay” path.\n- Prototype the hero, facts strip, gallery rhythm, trust block, and Guesty handoff at 390px first.\n- Validate the final concept against the five project routes and compare settled local and Vercel screenshots at the required viewports before presenting a preview."
      },
      {
        "id": "questions",
        "type": "markdown",
        "body": "## Further questions\n\n- Should the brand feel more like warm coastal editorial, quiet luxury, or relaxed family retreat?\n- Is there approved review content that can be used as direct-site proof?\n- Should the first Guesty interaction open availability immediately or after a short property overview?"
      },
      {
        "id": "caveats",
        "type": "markdown",
        "body": "## Caveats and assumptions\n\nThe 100-site pool is an inspiration census assembled from current public roundups and property sites, not a statistically representative sample. The fit score is a documented design heuristic; it does not claim access to traffic, revenue, accessibility audits, or conversion rates. Site ownership, design, and availability can change after the review date. Some candidates manage multiple units, but were included when their patterns transfer well to a single property."
      },
      {
        "id": "appendix_intro",
        "type": "markdown",
        "body": "## Appendix: all 100 researched candidates\n\nThis appendix preserves the full, deduplicated research pool so the shortlist can be challenged or expanded later."
      },
      {
        "id": "pool_table",
        "type": "table",
        "tableId": "pool100"
      }
    ]
  },
